[{"role": "user", "content": "Write a Python function that finds the longest palindromic substring."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "def longest_palindrome(s):
    if not s: return ""
    start = end = 0
    for i in range(len(s)):
        for l, r in ((i, i), (i, i + 1)):
            while l >= 0 and r < len(s) and s[l] == s[r]:
                l -= 1; r += 1
            if r - l - 2 > end - start:
                start, end = l + 1, r - 1
    return s[start:end + 1]

Expand around every centre, both odd and even; O(n^2) time, O(1) space."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Can you make it O(n)?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Yes, with Manacher's algorithm. It interleaves separators so every centre is odd, then reuses the mirror of the current rightmost palindrome to skip work already done. It's genuinely linear, but it's fiddly enough that I'd only reach for it if the quadratic version was actually too slow."}]

